I am applying for the Software Engineer 3, AI Builder Experience role at Mong=
oDB. At Black Piano, I developed a custom Model Context Protocol (MCP) tool t=
hat enables non-technical teams to turn a single-line prompt into publication=
-ready, data-grounded blog posts backed by automated pipelines. I also built =
a self-healing data-quality agent powered by Gemini that autonomously resolve=
s missing domain attributes via reference-table lookups with an LLM fallback,=
 writes verified records back to the dataset, retries three times on failure,=
 and triggers human-in-the-loop email escalation when unresolved.

Through my independent software engineering work, I build agentic developer t=
ooling and orchestration systems in Python and Node.js. I authored and publis=
hed MyLocalCLI on npm, a local-first terminal coding assistant featuring a St=
dio MCP bridge, forty-two built-in tools, dynamic skill injection, and parall=
el tool dispatch. In Python, I engineered JobAgents, a multi-agent harness th=
at orchestrates multiple CLI agents across external APIs and applies determin=
istic scoring across thousands of postings with zero model calls before deleg=
ating to language models.

MongoDB is ideally positioned to serve as the operational document and vector=
 foundation powering persistent state and memory for modern agentic applicati=
ons. I would welcome a conversation to discuss how my hands-on work with MCP =
tools and agent orchestration can support your builder experience team.

Prashanth Kumar Kadasi
kprsnt@live.com
https://kprsnt.in

